WEBVTT

01:41.000 --> 01:44.710
COUNTERATTACK SIGNAL

02:24.960 --> 02:25.920
<i>What the—?</i>

02:27.960 --> 02:29.800
<i>Why was I asleep?</i>

02:30.340 --> 02:31.760
<i>Ow...ow, ow, oww!</i>

02:31.920 --> 02:34.800
<i>Wait now.</i>
<i>What happened to me?</i>

02:36.760 --> 02:39.600
<i>I lost to a monster.</i>

02:40.350 --> 02:41.890
<i>Yet, I'm still alive.</i>

02:42.100 --> 02:43.100
<i>What's going on?</i>

02:44.940 --> 02:46.230
<i>And what happened to that kid?</i>

02:47.230 --> 02:50.690
<i>That ugly brat.</i>
<i>Did they let him go?</i>

02:51.110 --> 02:52.440
<i>Or don't tell me, they...</i>

02:54.200 --> 02:55.410
<i>It doesn't matter.</i>

02:55.530 --> 02:57.240
<i>I need to stop my bleeding.</i>

02:57.450 --> 02:59.620
<i>Actually...it's already stopped.</i>

03:00.160 --> 03:04.370
<i>Hm? My clothes are stuck to the wounds</i>
<i>and won't come off.</i>

03:04.500 --> 03:06.500
<i>They're completely fused together.</i>

03:07.080 --> 03:08.330
Now then...

03:29.440 --> 03:32.860
<i>The signal from</i>
<i>Dig-Here Doggie No.3 broke off.</i>

03:34.400 --> 03:36.820
<i>He found it.</i>
<i>Which means we're close.</i>

03:37.280 --> 03:39.030
<i>I should be able to</i>
<i>pinpoint their base soon.</i>

03:40.200 --> 03:43.290
Are we finally zeroing in
on their stronghold, Child Emperor?

03:43.620 --> 03:44.790
Mr. Sekingal.

03:45.540 --> 03:48.290
Tornado's been
pressuring us to hurry.

03:48.580 --> 03:50.420
Have the Class-S heroes gathered?

03:50.540 --> 03:51.670
Not all of them.

03:52.250 --> 03:55.300
Tank-Top Master and Metal Bat
are in the hospital.

03:55.880 --> 03:57.430
Drive Knight is missing.

03:57.590 --> 04:00.180
Watchdog Man and Metal Knight
have refused to participate.

04:00.300 --> 04:02.720
Not having everyone on board
this time really hurts.

04:02.850 --> 04:05.100
Zombieman is on his way here.

04:05.270 --> 04:07.690
We still haven't been able to
get in touch with...

04:08.020 --> 04:11.310
Silverfang, Demon Cyborg, and King.

04:11.980 --> 04:14.230
We plan to add all three
to the team.

04:15.070 --> 04:18.950
Class-S heroes are going to
be crucial to this operation.

04:19.780 --> 04:20.740
Wait a second.

04:21.070 --> 04:25.910
Actually, I did a bit of research
on Genos the Demon Cyborg.

04:26.330 --> 04:28.920
He lives in City Z's
ghost town, right?

04:29.250 --> 04:32.290
The Monster Association's hideout is
somewhere in the ghost town, right?

04:33.090 --> 04:36.340
Even the town he was born in
has disappeared from the map.

04:36.590 --> 04:38.340
Doesn't that sound suspicious?

04:38.550 --> 04:42.140
There are lots of heroes with
unknown origins or secrets.

04:42.140 --> 04:43.350
Why mention this now?

04:43.720 --> 04:46.850
We still know very little about
the enemy organization.

04:47.310 --> 04:49.890
The number and strength
of the monsters remain unknown.

04:50.310 --> 04:52.110
If there's a traitor among us

04:52.110 --> 04:55.360
our plans and infiltration routes
could be compromised.

04:55.570 --> 04:57.490
We might all be wiped out
if things go wrong.

04:57.900 --> 05:01.910
Genos is a newcomer and hasn't
proven himself to gain our full trust.

05:02.450 --> 05:04.830
<i>Don't trust anyone around you.</i>

05:05.370 --> 05:07.910
Are you worried he might betray us?

05:08.620 --> 05:10.920
If you have any doubts
just ask him directly.

05:11.500 --> 05:13.920
No, we shouldn't
share any information with him

05:13.960 --> 05:16.800
and he should be
entirely excluded from this operation.

05:18.510 --> 05:20.800
We can't afford
any more risk factors.

05:20.970 --> 05:22.680
But from a strategic standpoint...

05:23.470 --> 05:25.930
No, you're right.

05:26.390 --> 05:29.430
This is a rescue and sweep mission
we cannot afford to fail.

05:30.600 --> 05:33.310
Demon Cyborg is off the team.

05:34.060 --> 05:35.150
One more thing...

05:35.150 --> 05:38.610
I think it's odd that
Silverfang let Garou slip away.

05:39.150 --> 05:42.450
He must have held back because of
his attachment to his former disciple.

05:43.950 --> 05:48.120
It's been confirmed that Garou is allied
with the Monster Association.

05:48.330 --> 05:50.910
Unfortunately, we need to
remove Silverfang as well.

05:51.540 --> 05:52.830
Understood.

05:55.000 --> 05:56.920
But you need King, right?

05:57.170 --> 05:58.250
Of course.

05:58.250 --> 06:00.340
King is one of our key fighters.

06:00.840 --> 06:05.010
The hideout should be located soon.
Let everyone know.

06:05.890 --> 06:09.520
You're removing Silverfang and
Demon Cyborg from the operation?

06:09.680 --> 06:14.770
Yes. But instead, I'll gather
capable heroes from Class A to C

06:14.810 --> 06:16.610
and have them support Class S.

06:17.230 --> 06:20.070
They may lack in combat ability,
but it's better than nothing.

06:20.490 --> 06:23.110
If they can support Class S even slightly
that’s good enough.

06:23.200 --> 06:25.160
Don't treat them like
they're disposable!

06:25.320 --> 06:27.240
They could die!

06:27.410 --> 06:30.910
I don't expect everyone who goes in
to make it out alive.

06:31.080 --> 06:35.380
But that's a risk they accepted
when they chose the path of a pro hero.

06:35.750 --> 06:38.500
The life of a hostage is at stake.

06:38.750 --> 06:40.380
Some sacrifices are inevitable.

06:40.460 --> 06:44.380
Sekingal...Have you thought
about the consequences?

06:44.470 --> 06:48.680
If we lose more heroes to injury or death
we will be short-handed...

06:48.720 --> 06:50.260
Sitch, I remember that you were

06:50.260 --> 06:53.060
in charge of the Earthdoom Prophecy
Emergency Response Team.

06:53.560 --> 06:55.520
So I understand
where you're coming from.

06:56.060 --> 07:01.110
You want us to be prepared for a possible
worst-case scenario, right?

07:01.480 --> 07:01.650
EARTHDOOM

07:01.650 --> 07:04.240
EARTHDOOM
But I have
a different take on this.

07:04.240 --> 07:04.700
EARTHDOOM

07:04.700 --> 07:06.450
EARTHDOOM
The Monster Association itself is

07:06.490 --> 07:08.200
what the "Earthdoom" prophecy
was warning us about.

07:08.200 --> 07:08.780
what the "Earthdoom" prophecy
was warning us about.

07:09.530 --> 07:13.080
If left unchecked, they will
eventually destroy humanity.

07:13.540 --> 07:17.420
If that's the case, this is a
critical moment for the Hero Association.

07:17.830 --> 07:23.550
If we overcome this, we'll no longer live
in fear of that cursed prophecy.

07:23.970 --> 07:26.130
The future doesn't matter.

07:26.470 --> 07:30.300
In any case, I am the team leader
of the hostage rescue mission.

07:31.430 --> 07:35.980
Don't contact Silverfang and the others
behind my back. Got that?

07:38.150 --> 07:45.150
BUBBLE BUBBLE

07:47.070 --> 07:54.080
SIMMERING

08:07.220 --> 08:08.260
It's ready.

08:09.180 --> 08:10.220
SWISH

08:10.510 --> 08:14.560
SWISH SWISH SWISH

08:24.400 --> 08:25.230
FWIP

08:28.400 --> 08:29.240
SNATCH

08:30.450 --> 08:33.780
Why are you taking Master's meat,
Hellish Blizzard?

08:33.870 --> 08:35.750
Demon Cyborg Genos...

08:36.000 --> 08:38.830
Are you satisfied
being his sidekick?

08:39.040 --> 08:42.670
Stop it. Hot pots are meant to
be shared and enjoyed together.

08:42.710 --> 08:45.380
Hey, don't take all the tofu!

08:45.840 --> 08:46.880
Hang on a sec.

08:47.590 --> 08:50.720
You know, there's
something that's bugging me.

08:51.800 --> 08:55.390
Why are you guys acting like it’s totally
fine to eat someone else's hot pot?

08:56.270 --> 08:59.140
The napa cabbage is all gone.
Go home already.

08:59.270 --> 09:01.310
That's right.
Go home.

09:01.350 --> 09:02.360
It's cramped in here.

09:02.480 --> 09:03.440
That includes you.

09:03.520 --> 09:05.570
Silverfang I can understand.

09:05.690 --> 09:09.450
But a random old man has no business
hanging out with this group.

09:10.400 --> 09:13.530
If you want to join
the Blizzard Bunch

09:13.530 --> 09:16.160
you need to show me
you're worth it.

09:16.290 --> 09:17.200
SIZZLE

09:17.200 --> 09:19.250
SIZZLE
Huh? The Blizzard Bunch?

09:19.500 --> 09:21.830
You want me to annihilate you?

09:21.960 --> 09:24.210
Wait, Genos!
Don't break anything!

09:24.540 --> 09:26.250
Calm down, Genos.

09:26.300 --> 09:28.420
- This isn't like you.
- Right.

09:28.590 --> 09:33.010
I feel as though I've gotten to see
a new side of you.

09:33.010 --> 09:34.760
That makes me happy.

09:35.010 --> 09:39.020
You can forget about fighting,
share a hot pot, and speak openly here.

09:39.140 --> 09:41.350
You're lucky to have
good friends, Genos.

09:41.440 --> 09:42.440
Doctor...

09:43.310 --> 09:44.900
This woman is not my friend.

09:44.940 --> 09:46.610
"This woman"?
How rude.

09:46.650 --> 09:48.150
R-Really?

09:48.230 --> 09:50.610
But you're both heroes from
the same organization, right?

09:50.820 --> 09:53.030
Yes, but that's totally irrelevant.

09:53.360 --> 09:54.200
I see.

09:54.280 --> 09:58.540
<i>Wow... He's never disagreed with me</i>
<i>so adamantly.</i>

09:58.620 --> 10:00.790
<i>I just saw another side of him.</i>

10:00.870 --> 10:03.080
You said your name
is Kuseno, right?

10:03.670 --> 10:08.090
You’ve got impressive skills
crafting weapons for Demon Cyborg.

10:08.380 --> 10:12.220
We could hire you to develop weapons
for the Blizzard Bunch.

10:12.300 --> 10:17.390
Hey... If you insult Dr. Kuseno
any more, I'll incinerate you.

10:17.600 --> 10:20.100
Now, now. It's quite all right.

10:20.390 --> 10:21.640
Saitama.

10:22.100 --> 10:26.150
I wanted to ask you about
your thoughts on how to train disciples.

10:26.190 --> 10:29.570
Huh? My thoughts?
I don't really have any in particular.

10:29.820 --> 10:32.490
Where did I go wrong?

10:32.900 --> 10:35.620
Our dojo valued strength
more than anything else.

10:35.620 --> 10:37.580
Maybe that was wrong?

10:37.830 --> 10:38.990
Depends on the person.

10:39.200 --> 10:44.870
Hey Bang, don't start a long story
while Master Saitama is eating.

10:45.830 --> 10:47.000
Hey, Bang's brother.

10:47.460 --> 10:49.710
Stop hoarding the napa cabbage
and give some to Master.

10:53.010 --> 10:55.930
Hey, Kuseno.
Can you pass me the tea?

10:56.050 --> 10:58.930
Hey, don't tell the doctor
what to do.

11:02.140 --> 11:05.980
Kuseno, old man. Could you bring
some good meat next time, too?

11:06.100 --> 11:08.110
Stop making rude requests...

11:08.310 --> 11:10.150
I'm so sorry, Master!

11:11.190 --> 11:12.940
You should rest, Genos.

11:19.660 --> 11:22.500
Hard to relax with
so many people here.

11:22.660 --> 11:24.790
Once you're done eating
just go home, seriously.

11:25.250 --> 11:26.210
You too, King.

11:26.580 --> 11:28.630
Huh? How come you're lying down?

11:29.170 --> 11:30.800
Hey, don't fall asleep here!

11:31.050 --> 11:33.170
Hey, hey!

11:35.630 --> 11:36.630
He's dead.

12:06.120 --> 12:09.380
<i>An intruder...</i>
<i>In passage A-8...</i>

12:09.920 --> 12:11.630
<i>It's not a machine.</i>
<i>It's a living being.</i>

12:12.000 --> 12:13.960
<i>A monster who wants to join us?</i>

12:14.300 --> 12:16.630
<i>Or perhaps a scout from</i>
<i>the Hero Association?</i>

12:17.170 --> 12:19.470
<i>No, but to come here all alone...</i>

12:19.890 --> 12:22.140
<i>That's far too reckless.</i>

12:22.680 --> 12:26.730
<i>The final battle is approaching,</i>
<i>so I must verify this carefully.</i>

12:27.230 --> 12:28.100
Listen up.

12:28.190 --> 12:31.230
Looks like something's here again.
Go greet it.

12:31.520 --> 12:33.690
If it's a monster, bring it here.

12:34.070 --> 12:36.940
If it's anything else,
do whatever you want with them.

12:42.070 --> 12:45.410
Hey, wake up already!
It's morning.

12:46.330 --> 12:47.290
Hey!

12:48.750 --> 12:51.460
Hm? What am I doing here?

12:51.580 --> 12:53.670
You passed out fighting over meat.

12:54.040 --> 12:55.300
I thought you were a goner.

12:57.340 --> 12:58.630
Where are the others?

12:59.050 --> 13:00.840
I kicked them out after dinner.

13:01.340 --> 13:02.390
Genos is getting repairs.

13:02.680 --> 13:05.510
I-I see. I'm the only one
who stayed over?

13:05.510 --> 13:07.680
Sorry, Saitama.

13:08.230 --> 13:09.230
Don't worry about it.

13:09.690 --> 13:12.100
On your way out,
take the trash to the dump.

13:12.610 --> 13:15.480
It's in the residential area,
so it's kinda far from here.

13:16.730 --> 13:18.570
They're collecting
plastic bottles today.

13:21.110 --> 13:22.870
Wow, I slept really well.

13:23.620 --> 13:25.830
<i>What a peaceful</i>
<i>and refreshing morning</i>

13:25.830 --> 13:28.120
<i>with no noise from people or cars.</i>

13:29.040 --> 13:30.410
<i>A ghost town...</i>

13:30.830 --> 13:35.000
<i>They say the high monster</i>
<i>appearance rate drove people away</i>

13:35.340 --> 13:37.630
<i>but surprisingly,</i>
<i>I haven't run into any at all.</i>

13:38.380 --> 13:43.300
<i>Maybe Saitama living here actually</i>
<i>drove the monsters away.</i>

13:44.260 --> 13:46.890
<i>They say if you keep a cat in</i>
<i>a house infested with rats</i>

13:46.930 --> 13:48.970
<i>the rats will disappear.</i>

13:49.430 --> 13:53.230
<i>But...sometimes the rats are</i>
<i>just hiding in the attic.</i>

13:53.560 --> 13:57.360
<i>Maybe monsters are gathering</i>
<i>underground in nests instead...</i>

13:58.570 --> 14:01.820
<i>Yuck... Just thinking about it</i>
<i>gives me the creeps.</i>

14:05.200 --> 14:06.830
Hm? Hey, did you just...

14:07.870 --> 14:09.750
...come from
the other side of the fence?

14:09.830 --> 14:11.540
No, you must be imagining things!

14:13.710 --> 14:15.250
There, all done.

14:17.000 --> 14:20.380
<i>It's amazing that people still go to work</i>
<i>even in times like this.</i>

14:25.970 --> 14:28.640
Hm?
Someone's in front of my house.

14:29.310 --> 14:31.180
Oh! He's home!

14:31.930 --> 14:35.230
Thank god.
We've been waiting for you, King!

14:35.650 --> 14:38.570
We couldn't get in touch with you,
so we searched everywhere!

14:38.730 --> 14:40.320
<i>Oh, they're from the Association.</i>

14:40.480 --> 14:45.570
Oh, sorry.
My transmitter was broken during a fight.

14:45.780 --> 14:47.280
Where were you last night?

14:47.450 --> 14:49.240
Umm, City Z.

14:50.160 --> 14:51.580
Those stains on your clothes!

14:51.750 --> 14:53.910
Bodily fluids and flesh
from monsters?

14:53.960 --> 14:56.080
- This is from the hot pot ...
- You must've been in

14:56.080 --> 14:58.630
- Did I have any?
- an intense battle all night long.

15:00.130 --> 15:04.470
King, you must be exhausted
having fought without sleep or rest

15:04.510 --> 15:07.390
but we need you to accompany us
to the Headquarters at once!

15:14.810 --> 15:19.110
Captain Tongara said
he'd contact me every two hours

15:19.150 --> 15:22.480
but I haven't heard anything
from the unit all night.

15:23.030 --> 15:25.070
I assembled the best possible team

15:25.070 --> 15:27.110
and equipped them with
the finest weapons.

15:27.490 --> 15:28.820
Did the operation fail?

15:29.120 --> 15:30.330
Were they wiped out?

15:30.700 --> 15:33.200
Could they really be
defeated so easily?

15:33.580 --> 15:37.500
Even if the heroes head there,
won't they meet the same fate?

15:38.790 --> 15:39.750
Mr. Narinki.

15:41.250 --> 15:42.840
Looks like
you haven't slept all night.

15:43.460 --> 15:45.590
Why don't you go lie down
in the break room?

15:46.130 --> 15:50.800
Sekingal, my elite unit may
have been wiped out.

15:51.310 --> 15:52.350
This is terrifying.

15:52.600 --> 15:54.100
I have a bad feeling about this.

15:54.520 --> 15:56.980
At this rate,
we'll be crushed completely.

15:57.270 --> 15:58.270
Don't worry.

15:58.810 --> 16:02.520
I've told you before that
we will rescue your son.

16:03.030 --> 16:05.240
Please trust the Hero Association.

16:05.570 --> 16:07.610
Do we really have
a chance of winning?

16:08.110 --> 16:11.450
Metal Bat was defeated
even though he is a Class-S hero.

16:11.780 --> 16:13.790
I have no reason to trust you.

16:13.910 --> 16:16.660
You're not just putting on
a brave front, are you?

16:17.410 --> 16:19.460
Please...my son...

16:19.460 --> 16:22.290
You're his only hope.

16:22.840 --> 16:25.300
I'll give you as much
money as you want.

16:25.550 --> 16:29.180
Please! I just want to
see Waganma alive and well.

16:29.430 --> 16:30.970
For my son...!

16:31.180 --> 16:34.680
I'll give everything I own
to the Hero Association!!

16:34.850 --> 16:35.890
That won't be necessary.

16:36.560 --> 16:37.560
Who said that?

16:37.940 --> 16:41.560
Only those weaker than money
are swayed by it.

16:41.810 --> 16:46.070
People like that are useless
in a battle against monsters.

16:46.240 --> 16:47.240
Exactly!

16:47.780 --> 16:51.620
What's needed on the battlefield
is true courage to face evil.

16:51.990 --> 16:54.490
Isn't that what you're
trying to say, Flashy Flash?

16:54.700 --> 16:57.910
You're wrong.
Mindset is secondary.

16:58.160 --> 16:59.960
All that matters is strength.

17:00.080 --> 17:01.920
So just leave everything to me.

17:02.210 --> 17:06.630
Protecting the child is the top priority.
That's why we must act as a team.

17:06.960 --> 17:09.260
If it were just a matter of
taking them down like usual

17:09.260 --> 17:11.390
I'd have charged in with
my disciples long ago.

17:11.510 --> 17:14.180
Storming the monster hideout
with this team...

17:14.470 --> 17:16.060
Simple and straightforward.
I like it.

17:16.560 --> 17:19.770
I've been wanting to smash
an organization like this.

17:19.890 --> 17:24.400
I'll give everything I've got to bring
back that boy and my beloved inmates!

17:24.860 --> 17:27.070
I swear it on
this hand-knit sweater!

17:27.780 --> 17:29.570
I've located their hideout.

17:29.860 --> 17:31.990
All we need is King
and the backup team.

17:32.870 --> 17:33.370
We go in at noon.

17:33.370 --> 17:34.200
THE CLASS-S HEROES ARE HERE!!
We go in at noon.

17:34.200 --> 17:34.830
THE CLASS-S HEROES ARE HERE!!

17:34.830 --> 17:37.750
THE CLASS-S HEROES ARE HERE!!
We'll rescue the boy and
defeat the Monster Association.

17:37.750 --> 17:38.660
THE CLASS-S HEROES ARE HERE!!

17:38.750 --> 17:40.540
Don't worry about a thing
and get some sleep.

17:40.620 --> 17:43.290
By the time you wake up,
it'll all be over, old man.

17:43.460 --> 17:44.420
Hey now!

17:44.500 --> 17:47.170
Mr. Narinki is the Hero Association's
top advisor, you know!

17:47.550 --> 17:50.920
The Class-S heroes are going to have
a brief strategy meeting, right?

17:51.180 --> 17:52.300
Let's get going.

17:52.430 --> 17:54.600
I think I'll go lie down a bit...

17:54.800 --> 17:56.970
I'm leaving it all to you,
Sekingal.

17:57.180 --> 17:58.220
Yes, you can count on me!

17:59.520 --> 18:02.140
I'll give each of you
a map of the ghost town.

18:02.520 --> 18:04.900
I've confirmed
multiple entry points

18:04.900 --> 18:07.480
so we'll split up
and enter simultaneously.

18:07.900 --> 18:09.820
I'll explain route assignments now.

18:10.070 --> 18:12.860
We finally gathered everyone,
but we're gonna split up to fight?

18:13.070 --> 18:15.370
The monsters are doing the same.

18:15.490 --> 18:17.620
Staying in one group
risks total wipeout.

18:17.990 --> 18:20.830
I'll give each of you a transmitter
to track our positions.

18:23.290 --> 18:25.290
We need to prioritize
the hostage's safety

18:25.290 --> 18:26.920
so we need a
short, decisive battle.

18:27.090 --> 18:29.960
As long as even one of us
reaches the hostage, that's enough.

18:30.590 --> 18:32.970
The backup members will
wait aboveground.

18:33.380 --> 18:35.430
If any monsters try to escape
from underground

18:35.430 --> 18:36.890
they'll be there
to finish them off.

18:37.140 --> 18:40.100
Oh, like the Whack-A-Mole game.

18:40.270 --> 18:42.430
We can't have
a bunch of monsters

18:42.430 --> 18:44.350
spilling into
the residential areas again.

18:44.520 --> 18:46.230
About the backup members...

18:46.650 --> 18:49.360
We've been recruiting every
reasonably capable fighter available.

18:49.650 --> 18:51.400
They should be able to
handle monsters

18:51.400 --> 18:53.200
up to threat-level Tiger
without issue.

18:53.320 --> 18:55.360
Don't tell me you called Blizzard.

18:55.490 --> 18:58.700
Hm? Oh yeah,
I did reach out to her.

18:59.030 --> 19:01.160
Hellish Blizzard
is a valuable asset.

19:01.500 --> 19:03.290
She's already on her way here.

19:03.370 --> 19:08.040
Absolutely not. Don't put
my little sister in danger.

19:08.540 --> 19:11.380
If you drag her into this battle
I won't forgive you.

19:11.670 --> 19:14.300
With me here,
that's more than enough. Got it?

19:14.340 --> 19:16.340
- But...
- What is your answer?

19:16.640 --> 19:18.930
Uh, understood.

19:19.180 --> 19:21.930
I'll call her
and tell her to stand down.

19:28.310 --> 19:29.360
Good morning.

19:30.020 --> 19:33.110
Have you been behaving?
I've come to get  you.

19:33.400 --> 19:35.900
Just Tareo can step outside.
Let's go.

19:35.990 --> 19:38.660
What?! Why is he
the only one getting released?

19:38.700 --> 19:39.580
Not fair!

19:39.660 --> 19:42.160
Released? No, no.

19:42.200 --> 19:46.370
He's coming to my room.
So we can play.

19:47.120 --> 19:49.040
Well, you heard him.
You'd better go.

19:49.080 --> 19:52.590
N-No way!
I don't wanna! Help!

19:52.750 --> 19:56.260
Heroes! Hurry up
and save me, heroes!

19:56.340 --> 20:00.050
Um, I hate to tell you, but...

20:00.350 --> 20:04.350
The Hero Association is only trying
to rescue that kid over there.

20:04.810 --> 20:06.850
No one even knows you're here.

20:07.230 --> 20:10.190
No hero is ever coming to save you.

20:14.530 --> 20:19.780
Apparently, the monsters who went to
check on the intruder never came back.

20:20.030 --> 20:23.410
If they were killed then that means
the heroes have arrived?

20:23.870 --> 20:26.210
But we haven't heard any signal
to start the fight yet.

20:26.330 --> 20:29.040
According to Gyoro-Gyoro,
there's only one intruder.

20:29.120 --> 20:31.590
They're probably not affiliated
with the Hero Association.

20:33.710 --> 20:35.010
Look at this mess.

20:35.130 --> 20:38.340
Maybe that thing isn't even human,
after all.

20:38.800 --> 20:41.090
So that means the intruder
is a monster?

20:41.720 --> 20:46.060
Yeah, it could've been a
hot-tempered monster like King the Ripper.

20:46.230 --> 20:50.730
There are plenty of monsters out there
who hate the Monster Association.

20:51.020 --> 20:53.190
It'll be a pain
if things got chaotic

20:53.320 --> 20:55.530
before the showdown with
the Class-S heroes.

20:55.690 --> 20:59.780
Either way, just like Gyoro-Gyoro said
we need to deal with them pronto.

21:00.320 --> 21:03.120
By the way, where is King the Ripper?

21:03.280 --> 21:06.830
This is the perfect time for
a bloodthirsty psycho.

21:06.870 --> 21:08.370
Well, if he's not here

21:08.370 --> 21:10.500
then he's with the kid
he snatched yesterday.

21:10.620 --> 21:13.500
He probably can't hold
himself back anymore.

21:15.340 --> 21:18.590
Stop!

21:18.720 --> 21:21.550
Someone... Help me!

21:24.510 --> 21:26.720
Such a cute reaction.

21:27.100 --> 21:29.850
Why? Why are you doing this?

21:29.940 --> 21:33.060
Why? Because I'm a monster.

21:33.360 --> 21:37.610
Honestly, I couldn't care less
about this big war of theirs.

21:37.860 --> 21:42.030
I don't really need a new world
ruled by monsters.

21:42.240 --> 21:44.450
As long as I can unleash
my urge to shred flesh

21:44.450 --> 21:45.490
that's all I need.

21:45.580 --> 21:46.740
Stop...

21:46.990 --> 21:49.370
Killing is my only reason
for living.

21:49.450 --> 21:51.290
And right now,
I'm obsessed with you.

21:51.420 --> 21:52.710
H-Help!

21:52.790 --> 21:54.580
First, your tongue.

21:54.710 --> 21:58.050
Help...me!!

22:01.050 --> 22:02.010
It's...

22:05.260 --> 22:06.260
You!!

22:19.740 --> 22:21.070
Old dude!

22:21.990 --> 22:24.070
Come on, let's go, you little brat.

23:56.000 --> 24:00.890
MONSTER KING
